          "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b58251763b1cc9eb017468939687a729a6485350d4401a43e2cbfbe38e97c287",
          "source_text": "Since finite products, fibre products, equalizers, and final objects\nare limits over finite index categories we see that (1) implies both (2)\nand (3). By\nLemma <REF_0001>\nabove we see that (2) implies (1). Assume (3).\nNote that the product <MATH_0001> is the fibre product over the\nfinal object. If <MATH_0002> are morphisms of <MATH_0003>, then the\nequalizer of <MATH_0004> is\n<MATH_0005>\nThus (3) implies (2) and the lemma is proved.\n",
